---
import PublicLayout from '@/layouts/PublicLayout.astro'

const version = 'v1_2026-05-15'
const lastUpdated = '15 May 2026'
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Cookie Policy — Panda"
  description="Cookies and similar storage technologies used by Panda."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 md:px-6 md:py-16 prose prose-stone">
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-rich-earth/60">
      Version <strong>{version}</strong> &middot; Last updated {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <p>
      This page describes the cookies and similar local-storage technologies
      that Panda uses, and your choices around them. It supplements our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Kenya's Data Protection Act 2019
      treats cookie identifiers as personal data; we list every cookie we
      set so you can decide whether to allow them.
    </p>

    <h2>Strictly necessary</h2>
    <p>These are required for the site to function. They cannot be switched off:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>XSRF-TOKEN / panda_session</strong> — set by the Laravel API on form-submit pages (the contact form on this site). Anti-CSRF protection. Session-scoped.</li>
      <li><strong>__cf_bm</strong> — set by Cloudflare to distinguish humans from bots. 30 minutes.</li>
      <li><strong>cf_clearance</strong> — set by Cloudflare after passing a security challenge. Up to 30 days.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>App authentication (not cookies)</h2>
    <p>
      The Panda PWA at <a href="https://app.panda.shira.farm">app.panda.shira.farm</a>
      stores your authentication token in browser <strong>localStorage</strong>,
      not in a cookie. localStorage is similar technology and is covered by
      this Policy. The token is cleared on logout or when it expires.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics (planned, not yet active)</h2>
    <p>
      Panda does not currently use any third-party analytics provider. When
      we add analytics, we will use a privacy-friendly, cookie-less provider
      (e.g. Plausible) and update this Policy accordingly. If we ever switch
      to a provider that requires consent under DPA 2019, we will display a
      consent banner before any tracking cookie is set.
    </p>

    <h2>Marketing</h2>
    <p>Panda does not use marketing or advertising cookies.</p>

    <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
    <p>
      You can clear or block cookies through your browser settings. Doing so
      may break the contact form or trigger additional Cloudflare security
      challenges. Clearing localStorage will log you out of the PWA.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Questions: <a href="mailto:dpo@shira.farm">dpo@shira.farm</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</PublicLayout>
